# ─── Local operator consoles ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEVER commit these: this repo is PUBLIC. Canonical copies live in the PRIVATE
# repo at ../indiana-agenda-tracker/ops/.
#
# ⚠ MIP-8 (2026-08-29): the previous patterns did not do this. They were
#   /p168-ops.html
#   /*-ops.html
# and a leading slash anchors a pattern to the repo ROOT, while `*` never crosses
# a `/`. So both matched root only, and four consoles sat TRACKED and PUBLIC in
# mrd-ad682070b7/tests/ (p160-p163) for weeks. They were assessed at the time and
# carried no token and no URL the served build did not already publish — a broken
# guard, not a leak — and they were untracked (kept on disk) once copies existed
# in the private repo. ⛔ Untracking does not unpublish: they remain in this
# public repo's history, exactly like the old auth token.
#
# The pattern below is unanchored, so it matches at ANY depth. Keep it that way.
*-ops.html
